course: dictionary
lesson: 544
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Atomic» is one of these words. Atoms are the tiny particles that everything is made of, so atomic can mean to do with atoms.
explain: «Each GPS satellite keeps perfect time with an atomic clock.» Here atomic clock means a super-accurate clock that uses atoms. The words keeps perfect time are the clue.
explain: «Atomic bombs were dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaki.» Here atomic means to do with nuclear energy and weapons. Ask yourself: what kind of bomb is it? Then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Atomic comes from atom, the tiny particle that everything is made of.
fact: «Atomic» can mean to do with atoms, to do with nuclear energy, or a super-accurate clock that uses atoms.
fact: An atomic clock counts the ticks of atoms, so it keeps time very exactly.
fact: «Atomic» means to do with nuclear energy or nuclear weapons, as in «an atomic bomb».
fact: To pick the right meaning, read the other words in the sentence and ask what they tell you.
exercise: What are atoms? | *Tiny particles that everything is made of | Stars in the night sky | Long strings of letters | Big rocks in the ground
exercise: «Atomic bombs were dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaki.» What does atomic mean here? | To do with the sea and the tides | To do with plants and trees | *To do with nuclear energy and weapons | To do with tiny particles only, like dust
exercise: «Each GPS satellite keeps perfect time with an atomic clock.» What is an atomic clock? | A clock shaped like an atom | A clock that is always wrong | *A super-accurate clock that uses atoms | A clock that runs only at night
test: «Scientists date volcanic ash layers with natural atomic clocks in the rock.» What does atomic clocks mean here? | *Natural clocks that keep time using atoms | Clocks that stop when it rains | Clocks that show the date on paper | Clocks made of rock that never work
test: «An atomic power station makes electricity.» Which meaning fits best? | *To do with nuclear energy | To do with cooking food | To do with reading books | To do with the shape of a balloon
exam: Mia reads «atomic» in a science book about atoms and in a history book about bombs. Why does the same word mean different things? | Because the books were printed in different countries | Because history books use the wrong words | Because atomic always means the same thing | *Because the words around it give clues to its meaning
